{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17798": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physics",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Physics Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Assistant Professor of Physics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All application materials must be submitted electronically through Oberlin College and Conservatory's online application process at: https://jobs.oberlin.edu/ . A complete application will be comprised of: 1) A cover letter describing your teaching, scholarship, mentorship, and service, detailing how you contribute to an inclusive learning environment; 2) A Curriculum Vitae ; 3) Unofficial graduate and undergraduate transcripts; 4) Statement(s) on your teaching philosophy and expertise in diversity, equity, and inclusion; 5) A research statement that includes how you will support undergraduate research and how you would incorporate undergraduate students into your research program; and 6) Letters of Reference from three recommenders.* Suggestions for crafting effective application materials can be found at https://www.oberlin.edu/arts-and-sciences/departments/physics-and-astronomy/guidance-faculty-applicants . *By providing three letters of reference, you agree that we may contact your letter writers. Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 , and will continue until the position is filled. Completed applications received by the October 15 deadline will be guaranteed full consideration. Questions about the position can be addressed to: rowen@oberlin.edu , Rob Owen, Chair, or by phone at 440-775-8566. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Department of Physics & Astronomy at Oberlin College invites applications for a full-time tenure track faculty position in the College of Arts and Sciences in Physics, beginning fall of 2027. We are particularly interested in candidates with experience in experimental condensed matter, materials, or applied physics, in part to support engineering-related initiatives. We will also consider candidates with other research specialties provided that they would support robust undergraduate research projects. About Founded in 1833, Oberlin is a private four-year, highly selective national liberal arts college that is also home to an outstanding Conservatory of Music. Together, the two divisions enroll approximately 2900 students. The College views a diverse, equitable, and inclusive educational environment as contributing to the excellence of its academic program and was the first college in the US to admit Black Students and women. Among liberal arts colleges, Oberlin is a national leader in successfully placing graduates into PhD programs. Oberlin is situated on the outskirts of Cleveland, combining a cozy small-town atmosphere with the cultural amenities of a major city. The Cleveland Museum of Art, the Cleveland Orchestra, the Cinematheque, Karamu House, several educational institutions, and scores of restaurants, bars, music venues, and theaters add to the cultural and educational opportunities of the region. The Physics and Astronomy department graduates approximately 15 majors per year, with concentrations in either physics, astrophysics, or materials physics. The department has an authorized tenure/tenure-track faculty size of 7.5 full-time-equivalent. Faculty research interests include infrared molecular spectroscopy, novel magnetic nanomaterials, atomic physics, extragalactic chemical evolution & star formation, simulations of galaxy formation and supermassive black holes, numerical modeling of gravitational wave sources, and experimental particle physics. Approximately 80% of Oberlin’s Physics and Astronomy students do research during their time at Oberlin. This student research takes place during the semester, the summer, and Oberlin’s month-long Winter Term. Current faculty have a strong track record of maintaining external support, primarily through the RUI and MRI programs from the National Science Foundation. The Department and the College actively support new faculty with mentoring and professional development opportunities, as well as research through startup support and internal grants for conference travel and student research stipends. Completed applications received by the October 15 deadline will be guaranteed full consideration Responsibilities The incumbent will teach the standard teaching load (4.5 courses per year). Teaching assignments in our department typically span the entire undergraduate physics curriculum, including introductory and advanced courses for majors, lab courses as appropriate, and general-audience and seminar courses related to faculty interests. The incumbent will also be expected to engage in sustained scholarly research and/or other creative work appropriate to the position and participate in the full range of faculty responsibilities, including academic advising, mentoring undergraduate research and service on committees. The Department and College actively support new faculty with mentoring and professional development opportunities, including a paid pre-tenure leave for those on the standard six-year track, startup support, and internal grants for conference travel and research. Qualifications Among the qualifications required for appointment is the PhD degree (in hand or expected by first semester of academic year 2027-28). Candidates must demonstrate commitment to and potential excellence in undergraduate teaching, as well as the ability to perform high quality physics research. Oberlin is especially interested in candidates who can contribute to the distinctiveness and excellence of our academic community through their research, teaching, and service. The incumbent will bring understanding of or experience working with underrepresented and diverse academic populations. Oberlin recruits, employs, trains, compensates, and promotes regardless of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran’s status, and/or other protected status as required by law. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17728 Compensation Within the range established for this position, salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience and includes a competitive benefits package. Special Instructions to Applicants All application materials must be submitted electronically through Oberlin College and Conservatory’s online application process at: https://jobs.oberlin.edu/ . A complete application will be comprised of: 1) A cover letter describing your teaching, scholarship, mentorship, and service, detailing how you contribute to an inclusive learning environment; 2) A Curriculum Vitae ; 3) Unofficial graduate and undergraduate transcripts; 4) Statement(s) on your teaching philosophy and expertise in diversity, equity, and inclusion; 5) A research statement that includes how you will support undergraduate research and how you would incorporate undergraduate students into your research program; and 6) Letters of Reference from three recommenders.* Suggestions for crafting effective application materials can be found at https://www.oberlin.edu/arts-and-sciences/departments/physics-and-astronomy/guidance-faculty-applicants . *By providing three letters of reference, you agree that we may contact your letter writers. Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 , and will continue until the position is filled. Completed applications received by the October 15 deadline will be guaranteed full consideration. Questions about the position can be addressed to: rowen@oberlin.edu , Rob Owen, Chair, or by phone at 440-775-8566. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts Research Statement Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Affirmation of Diversity Statement Additional document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17559": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Education Programs Tutor-Student Worker Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Education Programs Tutor-Student Worker Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete this additional form https://oberlin.wufoo.com/forms/zgg9ao911834q1/ Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary Education Programs tutors work with children in grades Kindergarten through fifth grade (literacy) and ninth grade (math), within Oberlin City School District classrooms and community after school programs in Lorain County. Tutors work with children on literacy and/or mathematical concepts and includes tutoring and enrichment programming. Tutors may work with children in small groups or one-on-one, to support mathematics or in after school programs to assist with homework and enrichment activities. This is a paid position for Oberlin College students who have a Federal Work Study Award and are selected to work within this program, via a competitive application process. This position is also open to Bonner Scholars. Program Description: Tutors are hired, trained and placed within Oberlin City School District ( OCSD ) classrooms or community after school programs. Tutors work a consistent schedule based on the needs of teachers within OCSD , program directors in after school programs, and Oberlin College student academic and extra curricular schedule. Tutors are offered ongoing, paid (required) training opportunities and meetings to learn tutoring techniques, review state and local educational policy, student development, and professional development for career success. Tutors are required to complete a designated number of trainings and tutor group meetings and complete all surveys or reports requested by program staff. The Education program is directed by Susan Pavlus, Director of Education Programs at the Bonner Center. Responsibilities Report to assigned site/classroom during scheduled times, ready to engage with children and support literacy and/or mathematics • Sign in (electronically on Google Form) and out at site at each session and log in/out of Time Clock Plus application each work session • Attend group meetings and trainings • Report any absence to program staff, tutor leader, classroom teacher and/or site program director at least 2 hours before and via the preferred method of communication for each person • Spend tutoring time working with children on concepts and preparing for upcoming sessions with children • Provide documentation or information to classroom teacher, site director, tutor leader and program staff as requested, within the expressed time frame • Report any concerning behavior from children, as outlined within tutor training, and concerns regarding the supervision of children within school district or after school programs • Suggest resources and training topics to program staff and tutor leaders to best support working with children The Education Tutoring program functions within the OCSD during school hours, approximately 8:00 am until 3:15 pm, and within after school programs from 2:00-5:30 pm. Tutors, based on schedule and needs of the district and Lorain County after school programs, will be placed within grade levels and time frames that are mutually beneficial to the Oberlin College student, OCSD and Lorain County after school programs. Tutoring schedules must be consistent and weekly time commitments can range from 2-10 hours, depending on needs of OC student and school district and/or after school program. Schedules will be determined by program staff and communicated to student at the start of the semester, or shortly after being hired by the program. Qualifications Oberlin College students with Federal Work Study Awards and/or Bonner Scholars. The program will not accept volunteers who are fulfilling a court mandated volunteer experience. • Interest in working with children • Ability to follow through with program requirements, including training, surveys, and consistent work schedule • Background check required • Serve as a positive role model for students in Oberlin City Schools and community after school programs Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/14050 Compensation starting pay $14 per hour Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete this additional form https://oberlin.wufoo.com/forms/zgg9ao911834q1/ Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17332": {
      "title": "CHEM 254 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | CHEM 254 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry &amp; Biochemistry Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment CHEM 254 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must complete all of the “Availability” section of the application in order to be considered. Applications will be accepted until all positions are filled. Questions may be directed to either Dr. Cristinel Miinea, Chemistry & Biochemistry Laboratory Instructor and Manager (cmiinea@oberlin.edu) or Prof. Jason Belitsky, Associate Professor of Chemistry & Biochemistry (jbelitsk@oberlin.edu). Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for Teaching Assistants (TAs) for Fall 2026. There are openings for assisting CHEM 254 lab sections. Applicants must be pursuing an interest in the sciences in order to be considered (pursuing a major in chemistry or biochemistry is preferred, but not required). Chemistry & Biochemistry TAs will get the opportunity to develop their understanding of the materials at hand, gain further knowledge of topics that they previously learned, develop a professional relationship with new students, and develop their skills as educators. Responsibilities 5-7 hour/week commitment. Responsibilities include: • Prior knowledge and reasonable mastery of CHEM 254 material; • Availability to attend TA meetings on a weekly basis; • Assisting students in lab with relevant techniques and processes; • Assisting with the preparation of laboratory reagents and supplies. Qualifications You must be an enrolled student at Oberlin College & Conservatory to qualify. In order to be considered, applicants must have earned a passing grade in CHEM 254. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17331 Compensation $13.00-$13.75 depending on prior TA work experience in the department. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must complete all of the “Availability” section of the application in order to be considered. Applications will be accepted until all positions are filled. Questions may be directed to either Dr. Cristinel Miinea, Chemistry & Biochemistry Laboratory Instructor and Manager (cmiinea@oberlin.edu) or Prof. Jason Belitsky, Associate Professor of Chemistry & Biochemistry (jbelitsk@oberlin.edu). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Which afternoons are you available? (M-F 1:30-4:30 pm). (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17720": {
      "title": "Employment Operations Specialist",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Employment Operations Specialist Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Employment Operations Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary To manage and coordinate the employment process for the placement of qualified and diverse applicants for a variety of Oberlin College positions, including unionized staff. This position reports to the Director of People Analytics & HRIS . Responsibilities Duties and essential functions may include, but are not limited to, the following: Recruitment, Selection & Placement •         Assist with the recruitment, selection, and placement of candidates for hourly and salaried positions; process employment forms and documents; maintain employment records; and adhere to position posting procedures within the College’s collective bargaining agreements. •         Manage the College’s online applicant tracking system ( ATS ) and provide technical support to hiring managers and employees. •         Assist campus hiring managers with job postings in the ATS , external advertising, and adherence to union contracts. •         Train and assist campus hiring managers and staff on submitting job requests and navigating the online hiring process within the ATS . •         Coordinate the end-to-end hiring process workflow within the ATS . •         Develop and implement recruitment outreach strategies, including sourcing initiatives and community partnerships, to broaden applicant pools and support the College’s equal employment opportunity objectives. As a representative of Human Resources, maintain partnerships with external organizations (civic, social, professional, and other agencies) to identify potential candidates for employment opportunities. New Hire Support & International Employment •         Serve as a primary point of contact for newly hired College employees and assist them with completion of required employment documentation and onboarding activities within the ATS and external systems. •         Coordinate employment-related immigration processes for international employees by serving as liaison between incoming international staff, hiring managers, and the College’s immigration counsel to ensure proper visa status is obtained, required steps are completed, and expiring visas are proactively tracked. •         Generate appointment letters and Terms and Conditions of Employment offers. Compliance, Testing & Background Screening •         Assist the Human Resources department in ensuring compliance with EEOC policies and provide advisement regarding the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ) and accessibility requirements throughout the hiring process. •         Explain employment policies and procedures, applicable laws, and collective bargaining agreements to college departments, employees, and applicants. •         Manage employment testing for unionized positions, including scheduling, scoring, and selection processes. •         Ensure the issuance and completion of applicable background checks and reference checks for all new staff; inform departments of results. Temporary Workforce & Labor Relations Support •         Hire and manage a temporary employee pool of administrative assistants on campus, utilizing external hiring and/or agency options. Evaluate applications and resumes, conduct interviews, administer testing as needed, and recommend candidates to departments. •         Assist the Deputy Human Resources Officer with the hiring process for collective bargaining unit vacancies; attend Labor Management meetings to take minutes and provide updates on pending hires; communicate with union leadership regarding position postings; and track vacancies by union group. •         Manage the reclassification process for positions within the collective bargaining units by conducting reclassification interviews with employees. Additional Responsibilities •         Correspond and communicate with applicants and staff to ensure timely receipt of verbal and written information; answer questions and resolve issues related to employment, employee relations, compensation, benefits, and other human resource topics. •         Manage the annual service awards process and other employee award nominations. •         Assist in managing the college’s performance review platform. •         Perform related duties as assigned. Essential Job Functions Knowledge of: • Personal computer applications including word processing, spreadsheets, databases, and email. • Online applicant tracking systems. • Equal employment opportunity and affirmative action principles. Skill in: • Written and interpersonal communication, with the ability to communicate effectively with all components of the College and external constituents. • Written and verbal communication, including public speaking. • Working effectively in a high-volume, multi-task office environment. Ability to: • Gather, analyze, modify, and implement human resource information for both technical and non-technical users. • Work closely with internal customers and external consultants to coordinate successful operations in a professional manner. • Prioritize diverse tasks, meet deadlines, and remain results oriented. • Work independently in a self-directed manner. • Work effectively in a high-volume, multi-task office environment. • Act as a collaborative team member in a small human resources office, frequently assisting colleagues with projects and assignments for the success of the overall department. Marginal Job Functions Required Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field; or one year of additional relevant experience may be substituted for each year of the education requirement. • One to two years of human resources experience; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Desired Qualifications • Professional in Human Resources ( PHR ) certification is a plus but not required. • People Admin (Applicant Tracking System) experience preferred. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/4736 Compensation Commensurate with experience Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Please explain why you are interested in this position and provide details about any relevant experience. (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17804": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Staff Therapist Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Staff Therapist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary This is a full-time, 10-month position within a IACS -accredited department serving a residential campus of approximately 3,000 undergraduate students. The position operates within a short-term, evidence-informed clinical model consistent with IACS standards, which establish direct clinical contact as the primary function of all staff clinicians. CAPS serves a high-demand clinical environment. The person in this role is expected to maintain a direct clinical contact rate consistent with IACS accreditation standards, which establish 65% of compensated time as the upper threshold for sustainable direct-service load. Individual targets are set below this threshold to preserve capacity for crisis response, consultation, and case management. Responsibilities The following distribution reflects the expected allocation of professional time. IACS accreditation standards identify 65% direct clinical contact as the maximum sustainable threshold for staff clinicians. Individual clinical targets are established by the Director based on role responsibilities, caseload complexity, training responsibilities, and other non-clinical functions. Time allocations may be adjusted in response to clinical demand.. | Function | % Time | Direct Clinical Service | Up to 65% | Crisis and Access Coverage | 10% | Consultation and Coordination | 10% | Outreach and Programming | 10% | Administration, Training and Supervision | 5% Essential Job Functions Direct Clinical Service (Primary Function) Provide individual psychotherapy using time-limited, evidence-informed approaches aligned with CAPS scope of practice. Conduct clinical intake assessments, differential diagnosis, and short-term treatment planning. Co-facilitate group therapy offerings; Provide couples counseling as assigned; Maintain clinical documentation in the electronic health record (Medicat) in compliance with HIPAA , FERPA , and IACS standards. Crisis Intervention and Access Participate in walk-in triage rotation and provide same-day crisis assessment as scheduled. Contribute to on-call and after-hours crisis coverage in coordination with Campus Safety and Student Support. Coordinate post-hospitalization planning and follow-up care for students returning from inpatient psychiatric treatment. Operate within CAPS triage and routing protocols to match student need to appropriate level of care. Consultation and Campus Coordination Provide consultation to faculty, staff, families, and campus partners regarding student mental health concerns and appropriate referral pathways. Collaborate with Health Services, ODA , Campus Safety, and the Dean of Students office as needed to support high-risk students. Participate in cross-campus coordination structures as assigned by the Director. Outreach and Psychoeducation Develop and deliver psychoeducational programming and workshops for students, RAs, faculty, and staff. Support outreach efforts targeting historically underserved and marginalized student populations, including students of color, LGBTQIA+ students, students with disabilities, and first-generation students. Collaborate with campus partners on mental health promotion and prevention initiatives as clinical demand allows. Administration, Training and Supervision Complete clinical documentation and case management; participate in staff and training meetings; and provide supervision and mentorship to graduate-level practicum students as assigned. Marginal Job Functions Required Qualifications Master’s degree or higher in Counseling, Clinical Psychology, Social Work, or Marriage and Family Therapy from an accredited institution. Current independent licensure in mental health practice (Psychologist, LPCC , LISW , or MFT ) in the State of Ohio, or eligibility for licensure within 12 months of hire. Supervised clinical experience in a college counseling center or comparable mental health setting. Demonstrated competence in short-term, evidence-informed clinical modalities. Strong commitment to confidentiality, ethical practice, and compliance with HIPAA and FERPA . Demonstrated multicultural competence and ability to work effectively with diverse student populations. NOTE ON ACCREDITATION AND CLINICAL STANDARDS CAPS at Oberlin College holds accreditation through the International Accreditation of Counseling Services ( IACS ). IACS standards identify 65% of compensated time as the upper threshold for direct clinical contact. Individual clinical targets are set by the Director below or up to that threshold, as appropriate, based on caseload complexity, training responsibilities, crisis and access needs, and other non-clinical functions. Time allocation and workload are reviewed on an ongoing basis in accordance with accreditation requirements and departmental needs. Desired Qualifications Doctoral degree (Ph.D., Psy.D., Ed.D., or D.S.W.) in Counseling, Clinical Psychology, or Social Work. Completion of an APA -accredited doctoral internship. Experience with crisis intervention, post-hospitalization coordination, or high-acuity clinical populations. Training or experience in the treatment of substance use disorders or co-occurring conditions. Experience working with students of color, LGBTQIA+ students, first-generation students, and other underrepresented groups. Familiarity with electronic health record systems and clinical data practices. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17673 Compensation Commensurate with experience Special Instructions to Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17568": {
      "title": "Media Associate",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Media Associate Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Media Associate Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Studio Art Media Lab Associate position is available for students who have a familiarity with or interest in working with digital and analog technologies. Students with skills in video, audio, photography, printing, interactive media, projection mapping, micro-controllers, coding and other areas are all welcome to apply. The successful candidate will be available 6 (min)-12 (max) hours a week. In addition to this, the Media Associate may occasionally provide drop-in assistance to fellow students, help develop and deliver multimedia workshops, and assist faculty in their courses. Punctuality, leadership, work ethic, and approachability are required. The successful candidate will feel confident in troubleshooting equipment and pursuing answers to students’ technology questions. Responsibilities Test and organize, assist students with technology in Studio Art labs, and collaborate with the Media Manager on keeping equipment inventory. Qualifications Media Lab Associate must be a student enrolled at Oberlin College with skills and interest in creative technologies. Examples include: Software: Adobe Creative Cloud Reaper, Logic Pro, or other DAWs Processing, Sketchup Unity, Blender Hardware: Video Recording/Playback (incl. older camcorders & VHS ) Sound recording Arduino, Raspberry Pi Projectors Large-format Printers Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17567 Compensation $13.00 Special Instructions to Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Have you previously worked as a student employee in any capacity on the Oberlin College campus before? Yes No Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17352": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Systems Administrator Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Systems Administrator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Center for Information Technology ( CIT ) at Oberlin College invites applications for a Systems Administrator to provide hands-on support across enterprise server and network infrastructure. Reporting to the Manager of Network Infrastructure, this full-time, 12-month Administrative and Professional Staff position is responsible for advancing major technology institutional initiatives, including enterprise technology modernization, strengthened cybersecurity, and transformative digital experiences that support teaching, learning, research, and student success. Joining CIT means becoming part of a collaborative, mission-driven technology team that values innovation, service, and continuous improvement. Team members have the opportunity to make meaningful impact, grow professionally, and help shape the future of technology at a leading liberal arts institution. Responsibilities Role Focus This role centers on technical excellence, reliability, organization, and collaboration in managing both enterprise systems and network infrastructure. The successful candidate will bring: At least five (5) years of hands-on enterprise experience A strong spirit of teamwork and service Excellent organization and documentation practices The ability to support both systems administration and network administration in a dynamic environment Core Responsibilities Administer and maintain Windows server infrastructure to ensure availability, performance, and security. Support network infrastructure, including switching, routing, firewalls, and connectivity services. Monitor system and network performance, capacity, and reliability. Troubleshoot complex infrastructure issues in partnership with vendors and internal teams. Maintain Active Directory, Group Policy, Windows servers, and application services. Support virtualization, storage, and Microsoft SQL Server environments. Implement and maintain backup, disaster recovery, and monitoring solutions. Maintain accurate technical documentation, architecture diagrams, and operational procedures. Participate in maintenance windows and occasional after-hours response. Contribute to a collaborative, service-focused IT culture that supports the Oberlin community. Essential Job Functions Marginal Job Functions Required Qualifications Minimum five (5) years of hands-on experience in enterprise systems and network administration . Strong expertise in: Active Directory, Windows Server, and enterprise application hosting Virtualization platforms (e.g., VMware) Enterprise backup and recovery solutions (e.g., Veeam) Network infrastructure including switching, routing, firewalls, VLANs, and secure connectivity Proficiency in PowerShell, Python, or similar automation tools . Solid understanding of: Server and network security best practices Monitoring, logging, and performance optimization Capacity planning and disaster recovery Familiarity with hyperconverged infrastructure and modern data center environments. Demonstrated organizational strength, attention to detail, and documentation discipline. Proven ability to collaborate effectively within a team while managing priorities independently. Knowledge of secure remote access technologies and IT security principles. Desired Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience with cloud identity and productivity platforms (Microsoft Entra ID, Google Workspace, Okta). Experience in higher education or similarly complex enterprise settings . Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17220 Compensation Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Compensation includes an excellent benefits package including tuition benefits for eligible children to attend Oberlin College and many other institutions. Special Instructions to Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17723": {
      "title": "Audiovisual Equipment Assistant Fall 2026",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Audiovisual Equipment Assistant Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Audiovisual Equipment Assistant Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Go to Student Employment website to fill out appropriate tax forms Click “Information for Students.” Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary Assist patrons with equipment rental needs and usage for class projects and organizational events. Prepare and return equipment orders. Track inventory accessories on items such as camera kits, lighting kits and audio kits. At times, you may be required to deliver, set-up, and operate AV equipment for campus use. This includes projectors, screens, document cameras, sound systems, TV carts, etc. You will be testing equipment, answering phones, creating and packing orders, assisting with invoicing, and general office work. You may be required to demonstrate and explain general functionality of AV’s cache of equipment. Responsibilities Must be reliable, prompt, and organized. Qualifications Must be willing to learn; training will be provided. You must be an enrolled Oberlin College student. First and second years encouraged to apply due to progressively increasing responsibilities and opportunites for independent work. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17667 Compensation $14.25 an hour Special Instructions to Applicants Go to Student Employment website to fill out appropriate tax forms Click “Information for Students.” Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
