    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17596": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Faculty Vacancy in Opera Theater Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Faculty Vacancy in Opera Theater Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on October 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Those received after that date may be considered until the position is filled. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Oberlin Conservatory invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in Opera Theater beginning in the 2027-28 academic year. About The Oberlin Conservatory of Music, founded in 1865, is the nation’s oldest continuously operating conservatory, and the only major music school in the country linked with a preeminent liberal arts college. Students are enrolled in undergraduate programs leading to the Bachelor of Music in performance, jazz studies, composition, technology in music and related arts, recording arts and production, music theater, and musicology. Oberlin also offers graduate programs leading to the Master of Music in conducting, the Master of Music in performance on historical instruments, the Master of Fine Arts in piano technology, and artist diplomas. Responsibilities Direct mainstage operas Teach opera workshop classes, in collaboration with music director/pianist Teach seminar in opera directing and/or other opera courses as expertise and interest allow Oversee opera budget, in collaboration with the conservatory finance manager Coordinate design process and all production personnel for the mainstage operas, in collaboration with the theater department Coordinate mainstage repertoire selection process, in collaboration with voice faculty, opera staff and theater personnel Qualifications Outstanding record of professional experience as an opera director Advanced degree in opera theater, theater, or equivalent experience Experience as a lyric theater director or equivalent performance experience; musical and linguistic expertise Practical knowledge of theater technology Experience teaching acting and/or movement to singers Demonstrated success in working effectively and collaboratively with faculty, staff and students Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17578 Compensation Oberlin College offers a competitive compensation package with excellent benefits. Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin on October 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Those received after that date may be considered until the position is filled. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/16659": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Administrative Assistant - Temp Pool Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Administrative Assistant - Temp Pool Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants would need to be available to work sporadically and may have periods in which there are no assignments available. This a temporary pool position to cover for those on leave of absence or for other vacancies. Applicants who meet the required qualifications will be brought in for computer testing (keyboarding, MS Word & Excel) after their application has been reviewed. Temporary administrative assistants who perform well, have been hired into FT positions at Oberlin College. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary Oberlin College is recruiting temporary administrative assistants for the administrative temp pool. The administrative assistants work assignments with varying lengths of time in any office within the College and may experience periods of time in wait for the next assignment. If you enjoy a challenge and want to provide support to different areas on our beautiful campus, this is something that might interest you. We are looking for seasoned administrative staff who may enjoy short or long term assignments. Responsibilities Flexible duties which may include the following: Serve as receptionist (answer the telephone, handle mail, send and receive faxes and emails, provide message service, greet and direct students and visitors) Create, organize and maintain departmental records and files. Compose routine correspondence; prepare and edit announcements and/or publications. Assist in organizing departmental events; schedule appointments; make arrangements for meetings including scheduling rooms and catering. Maintain office equipment and inventory of office supplies; initiate requisitions for materials and supplies. Maintain departmental or project budgets and accounts including payment of invoices, reimbursements and related budget assistance; maintain petty cash; prepare payment requests. Maintain and update website. Oversee student employees; initiate and prepare forms and records including student payroll. Qualifications High school diploma with at least three years recent office experience in a fast-paced office setting; possess strong interpersonal and verbal and written communication skills; thorough knowledge of proper grammar, spelling and punctuation, office methods, procedures and practices; keyboarding speed of 40 wpm with emphasis on accuracy; proficiency in word processing (Microsoft Word) and spreadsheet programs (Microsoft Excel); attention to detail; familiarity with database software; must demonstrate skills and abilities specific to the position assignment. Testing required prior to interview: Keyboarding (typing speed and accuracy): 40 wpm MS Basic Word, MS Excel Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/16646 Compensation Compensation is commenserate with knowledge and experience. Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants would need to be available to work sporadically and may have periods in which there are no assignments available. This a temporary pool position to cover for those on leave of absence or for other vacancies. Applicants who meet the required qualifications will be brought in for computer testing (keyboarding, MS Word & Excel) after their application has been reviewed. Temporary administrative assistants who perform well, have been hired into FT positions at Oberlin College. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you willing to work a flexible work schedule and short assignments? (Open Ended Question) What website directed you to the Oberlin College job site? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17806": {
      "title": "Departmental Technician Il",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Departmental Technician Il Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Departmental Technician Il Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants chosen for an interview will be contacted to take Keyboarding, Microsoft Word, and Excel tests in the Office of Human Resources prior to the scheduling of interviews. Candidates must pass all tests in order to be eligible for an interview. This position is available to both internal Ocope members and external candidates, with current members receiving preference during the first 10-days, expiring September 13, 2026. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Office of the Center for Student Success invites applications for the position of Departmental Technician Il. This is a full-time, Administrative Assistant position, working a 12-month schedule, reporting to the Dean of Student Success. All Administrative Assistant positions in the Center for Student Success serve as members of the staff team supporting the overall operations of the office. Responsibilities The incumbent will have general responsibility for providing proactive and timely administrative and operational support to the Center for Student Success ( CSS ) Essential Job Functions Operations ● Serve as the first point of contact for current and prospective students, parents, faculty, staff, alumni, and the general Oberlin community regarding the Center for Student Success initiatives. Create a safe, tidy, welcoming, and inclusive space (including the CSS suite and student lounge) for all CSS visitors and guests. ● Maintain the CSS departmental and event calendars: coordinate staff schedules, plan meetings, schedule appointments, and coordinate conference room and student lounge scheduling. ○ Make adjustments to the operations as needed. ● Assist in the management and archiving of office and departmental files, both public and confidential. ○ Maintain, update, and revise confidential student files in institutional databases such as Banner, ENGAGE , etc. ○ Assist in the maintenance and organization of the CSS Box folders and the files therein. ● Manage budgetary and tracking oversight: supply the Dean of Student Success and Leadership Team members with regular updates on budget/fund changes; compare purchases to planned expenditures; monitor spending; create and distribute annual budgetary templates. ● Manage staff mail and directory; update and distribute staff phone lists. ● Maintain the CSS Operations Manual and provide input in the review and implementation of departmental operations and procedures. ● Manage office supply inventory and monthly departmental supply orders. ● Coordinate office maintenance issues with the department of Facilities, including submitting maintenance requests and scheduling facilities work orders. Responsible for communicating to CSS staff the timelines of such work orders and schedules for repairs. ● Provide primary support for all CSS -related office equipment, including maintenance, repair, and purchasing. ○ Develop and manage a system for logging all CSS departmental equipment and the maintenance thereof. ● Provide administrative and operational assistance for CSS departmental participation in Oberlin events: Orientation, Welcome Week, Winter Term, Commencement, and other institution-wide events. ● Attend monthly divisional Managers and Administrative Assistants meetings. ○ Attend other events and meetings as necessary; take notes as needed. Communications ● Serve as the first point of contact for current and prospective students, parents, faculty, staff, alumni, and the general Oberlin community regarding the Center for Student Success initiatives. Respond to questions from faculty, staff, students, families, and the general public about the department’s services and Oberlin in general: ○ Be knowledgeable about the basic operations of the entire department and respond personally to requests for information in a timely manner; articulate the work of the department to other constituencies. ○ Address questions requiring interpretation and explanation and refer non-routine questions or complaints (including difficult student crisis situations) to appropriate staff. ● Coordinate office communications: ○ Answer and screen telephone calls; manage department voicemail and email; manage departmental out-of-office messaging. ○ Compose, proofread, and edit departmental correspondence and communications: inclusive of physical (posters, signs, flyers) and virtual (Campus Digest, Engage, and Instagram) messaging. ○ Assist in the composition and distribution of departmental reports, requiring knowledge of the college and institutional policies and procedures. ○ Assist in the maintenance of the departmental website and bulletins. ○ Prepare files for print, support social media accounts, and maintain departmental bulletin boards. Marginal Job Functions Core Function Support ● Provide general secretarial and administrative support for the Dean of Student Success ( DSS ). ○ Assist the DSS in maintenance of their calendar: schedule meetings and manage logistics; reserve meeting rooms, maintain guest lists, manage Zoom logistics, and coordinate guest schedules. ○ Provide administrative support for candidate searches: maintain applications and related files, prepare acknowledgment letters, schedule meetings, coordinate communications with search committee members, and make candidate travel arrangements. ● Assist other staff members in the office as needed: ○ Provide bi-annual clerical support to the Learning Enhancement Across the Disciplines ( LEAD ) program by assisting with faculty outreach, course management, and section building. ○ Provide communications and operations support to the Learning and Development core function through email campaigns, print orders, and social media management as needed. Assist in student outreach and codes management. ○ Email students for Success coaching appointment reminders, follow-ups, survey outreach, and more. ○ Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications College degree or equivalent combination of experience and education, 5-7 years of office experience with a high volume of public contact; demonstrated ability to function effectively, efficiently and appropriately in a rapid-paced environment, high level of customer service experience; ability to interact well with a diverse range of individuals, including students, staff, and faculty; demonstrated ability to perform detailed work with a high degree of accuracy, and the ability to respond to pressures, deadlines and changes in priorities and schedules; excellent verbal and written communication skills; experience demonstrating initiative and good judgment; a minimum keyboarding skill of 40 wpm with emphasis on accuracy (test at time and place of application); demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, and multi-level database management systems; and favorable references. All staff at the Center for Student Success display a deep commitment to educational equity and the advancement of underrepresented or marginalized groups in educational spaces, and will commit to partaking in ongoing professional development opportunities towards this goal. Desired Qualifications Bachelor’s degree; experience with Google suite and Box preferred; experience with educational technology platforms preferred (Blackboard, Curriculog, ENGAGE , Presence etc.), familiarity with Oberlin College and Conservatory. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17778 Compensation This Pay Grade 7 Administrative Assistant position is to be filled at an hourly rate of $30.04 or the appropriate transfer rate for internal candidates and includes an excellent benefits package. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants chosen for an interview will be contacted to take Keyboarding, Microsoft Word, and Excel tests in the Office of Human Resources prior to the scheduling of interviews. Candidates must pass all tests in order to be eligible for an interview. This position is available to both internal Ocope members and external candidates, with current members receiving preference during the first 10-days, expiring September 13, 2026. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References Affirmation of Diversity Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * The Center for Student Success is a high-traffic environment serving students, families, faculty, staff, and other members of the Oberlin community. Describe how you would manage a situation in which a student is visibly upset at the front desk, the phone is ringing, a parent is waiting for assistance, and a staff member needs immediate administrative support. How would you determine what requires immediate attention, what can wait, and what should be referred to another staff member? (Open Ended Question) * The Center for Student Success serves students with a wide range of backgrounds, identities, experiences, and needs. How have you worked to ensure that the people you serve feel welcomed, respected, and supported? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17381": {
      "title": "Community Based Work Study Student Position",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Community Based Work Study Student Position Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Community Based Work Study Student Position Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Additional application required: https://oberlin.wufoo.com/forms/z1p4oqr61suu766/ Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary Description: The Oberlin Community Based Work Study Program hires Oberlin College students with a Federal Work Study Award to work within community organizations in Oberlin. Each year Oberlin College hires students to work at over 16 community partners, serving the Oberlin community through work at non-profit organizations that serve a variety of needs like food insecurity, the arts, historical organizations, city government, business collaboratives, education, and other community identified needs. Responsibilities Hired students will elect to apply to one of the following organizations, serving in a variety of roles. A brief description of the organization is included below: America Counts: Math Tutoring grades K-8 America Reads: Reading Tutoring grade K-5 City Fresh: Fresh fruit and vegetable distribution organization Firelands Association for the Visual Arts ( FAVA ): Studio art classes and gallery space Illuminating Nations Through Offering an Opportunity ( INTO ): Fair Trade organization Kendal at Oberlin: Retirement community, includes roles in arts and engagement with residents Legion Field: Community garden Mad Factory (Music, Arts, Drama): Theater organization Ninde College Access Program: College access work in local high school Northern Ohio Youth Orchestra ( NOYO ): Youth Orchestra programming Oberlin Community Services: Social services organization and food bank Oberlin Heritage Center: Historical programming Office of Sustainability: City of Oberlin office (non-partisan work) Our Whole Lives: Health programming for middle and high school students Western Reserve Land Conservancy: Land preservation and management Wilson Bruce Evans House Historical Society: Historical site and history preservation And other organizations to be added later. Qualifications Oberlin College student on-campus Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17380 Compensation $12-14 per hour, varies by organization Special Instructions to Applicants Additional application required: https://oberlin.wufoo.com/forms/z1p4oqr61suu766/ Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17730": {
      "title": "Director of Information Security",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Director of Information Security Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Director of Information Security Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Commitment to Equal Opportunity and Inclusive Excellence : Oberlin College is committed to creating and sustaining a vibrant, welcoming community where all individuals are treated with dignity and respect, and where every member has an equal opportunity to learn, work, and contribute based on their talents, skills, and merit. We value a campus environment that draws on a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, perspectives, and ideas to enrich education, scholarship, and daily interactions. The College adheres strictly to all applicable federal and state civil rights laws, including Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, the Equal Protection Clause, and related regulations. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected characteristic in employment, admissions, or educational programs. Hiring and advancement decisions are made based on qualifications, experience, and job-related criteria. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds who share our dedication to academic excellence, free inquiry, respectful dialogue, and equal opportunity under the law to apply. The Office for Institutional Equity plays a key role in supporting a fair, compliant, and inclusive workplace and learning environment for the entire Oberlin community. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Center for Information Technology ( CIT ) invites qualified applicants for the position of Director of Information Security, a strategic leadership role responsible for advancing Oberlin College & Conservatory’s enterprise cybersecurity program. This is a full-time, on-campus leadership position based in Oberlin, Ohio, requiring regular in-person engagement to lead cybersecurity initiatives and collaborate with campus stakeholders. This role joins Oberlin at a pivotal moment as the College undertakes a significant digital transformation, including implementation of Workday, modernization of enterprise systems, expansion of cloud technologies, and the responsible exploration of artificial intelligence (AI). The Director of Information Security will provide the strategic vision, operational leadership, and technical expertise necessary to protect the College’s information assets while enabling innovation, academic excellence, research, and institutional success. Reporting to the Chief Information Officer ( CIO ), the Director is responsible for leading the College’s cybersecurity strategy, governance, security operations, risk management, incident response, regulatory compliance, and cyber resilience initiatives. Serving as the principal advisor on cybersecurity, privacy, AI risks governance, and emerging technologies, the Director ensures that security is integrated into institutional planning, technology modernization, and enterprise decision-making. Working collaboratively with CIT members, the Office of General Counsel, Human Resources, Finance, Academic Affairs, faculty, staff, students, and external partners, the Director develops and leads a modern, risk-based cybersecurity program that safeguards institutional data, technology resources, research, and digital services while supporting Oberlin’s mission of teaching, learning, creativity, and service. Responsibilities See Below: Essential Job Functions Strategic Leadership & Governance Serve as a member of the CIT Leadership Team and contribute to the College’s technology strategy, digital transformation, and institutional planning. Develop, implement, and continuously evolve the College’s enterprise cybersecurity strategy, roadmap, governance framework, policies, standards, and procedures. Advise on cybersecurity risks, AI risks governance, privacy, regulatory compliance, enterprise risk management, and emerging technologies. Present cybersecurity strategy, institutional risk posture, program maturity, and security metrics to executive leadership and governance committees. Establish meaningful cybersecurity performance metrics and executive dashboards that demonstrate institutional risk reduction and program effectiveness. Cybersecurity Operations & Technology Lead the College’s enterprise cybersecurity operations, including security monitoring, threat detection, identity and access management ( IAM ), endpoint detection and response ( EDR ), cloud security, network security, email security, vulnerability management, incident response, and security architecture. Develop, implement, and continuously improve a comprehensive cybersecurity program focused on preventing, detecting, responding to, and recovering from cyber threats. Ensure cybersecurity is integrated into enterprise infrastructure, cloud platforms, identity services, Workday, Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, and other enterprise applications throughout their lifecycle. Lead enterprise vulnerability management, threat hunting, ransomware protection, malware prevention, detection engineering, and remediation of security risks across on-premises and cloud environments. Direct continuous monitoring and improvement of the College’s external security posture through attack surface management, security ratings, and operational performance metrics. Lead cyber incident response, cyber crisis management, business continuity, disaster recovery planning, tabletop exercises, and post-incident reviews. Evaluate, implement, and optimize cybersecurity technologies and security controls, including security automation, email authentication ( SPF , DKIM , DMARC ), anti-phishing technologies, and emerging security capabilities. Risk Management, Compliance & Legal Partnership Lead the College’s enterprise cybersecurity risk management program and ensure compliance with applicable regulatory requirements and industry frameworks, including FERPA , HIPAA , GLBA , PCI DSS , NIST Cybersecurity Framework, and CIS Controls. Partner closely with the Office of General Counsel on cybersecurity, privacy, technology contracts, records preservation, breach response, litigation readiness, and regulatory compliance. Oversee third-party and vendor cybersecurity risk assessments and participate in technology procurement and contract reviews. Support cybersecurity audits, cyber insurance renewals, and institutional risk assessments. Data Protection & AI risks Governance Lead institutional initiatives related to data classification, data protection, data loss prevention ( DLP ), and information governance. Develop and support policies for the responsible, secure, and ethical use of artificial intelligence. Assess cybersecurity and privacy risks associated with AI and other emerging technologies while enabling responsible innovation. Leadership & Collaboration Build strong partnerships across academic and administrative units to promote cybersecurity as a shared institutional responsibility. Develop and oversee a comprehensive cybersecurity awareness and education program for faculty, staff, and students, including phishing simulations, role-based training, and executive awareness initiatives. Partner with faculty, research leadership, and grant administrators to protect research systems and data while supporting applicable research security and compliance requirements. Develop and manage the Information Security operating and capital budgets, prioritizing investments based on institutional risk and strategic priorities. Recruit, lead, mentor, evaluate, and develop cybersecurity professionals while fostering a collaborative, service-oriented, and high-performing culture. Build trusted relationships with executive leadership, faculty, staff, students, and external partners while effectively communicating cybersecurity risks in business terms. Represent Oberlin in higher education cybersecurity organizations and maintain awareness of emerging threats, evolving regulations, and industry best practices. Marginal Job Functions Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Cybersecurity, Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related field. Five (5) years of progressively responsible cybersecurity experience, including leadership of enterprise information security programs and direct responsibility for cybersecurity strategy, operations, and risk management. Experience working in a higher education environment or a similarly complex, mission-driven organization with diverse stakeholder groups and shared governance. Demonstrated hands-on experience in cybersecurity operations, including security architecture, governance, risk management, cloud security, identity and access management, vulnerability management, incident response, and enterprise security technologies. Demonstrated experience securing hybrid and cloud environments, including Microsoft 365, Azure, Google Workspace, identity platforms, and enterprise SaaS applications. Demonstrated ability to lead complex, cross-functional cybersecurity initiatives and technology transformation projects. Experience collaborating across technical and non-technical teams and effectively communicating cybersecurity concepts to executive leadership, faculty, staff, and institutional stakeholders. Strong knowledge of cybersecurity frameworks and standards, including NIST Cybersecurity Framework, CIS Controls, Zero Trust principles, and applicable regulatory requirements. CISSP certification required (or the ability to obtain certification within one year of hire). Desired Qualifications Master’s degree in Cybersecurity, Information Technology, Computer Science, Business Administration, or a related field. Experience supporting cybersecurity programs in higher education. CISM , CRISC , GIAC , or similar advanced cybersecurity certifications. Experience securing Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, Azure, Workday, and other enterprise SaaS platforms. Experience implementing Zero Trust architecture, identity governance, cloud security technologies, and modern security operations. Experience leading cybersecurity programs through enterprise digital transformation initiatives, including cloud modernization. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17689 Compensation Salary will commensurate with qualifications and experience. Special Instructions to Applicants Commitment to Equal Opportunity and Inclusive Excellence : Oberlin College is committed to creating and sustaining a vibrant, welcoming community where all individuals are treated with dignity and respect, and where every member has an equal opportunity to learn, work, and contribute based on their talents, skills, and merit. We value a campus environment that draws on a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, perspectives, and ideas to enrich education, scholarship, and daily interactions. The College adheres strictly to all applicable federal and state civil rights laws, including Title VI, Title VII , Title IX, the Equal Protection Clause, and related regulations. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected characteristic in employment, admissions, or educational programs. Hiring and advancement decisions are made based on qualifications, experience, and job-related criteria. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds who share our dedication to academic excellence, free inquiry, respectful dialogue, and equal opportunity under the law to apply. The Office for Institutional Equity plays a key role in supporting a fair, compliant, and inclusive workplace and learning environment for the entire Oberlin community. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17615": {
      "title": "Endpoint Support Specialist (Mac & Linux)",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Endpoint Support Specialist (Mac &amp; Linux) Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Endpoint Support Specialist (Mac & Linux) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the application on jobs.oberlin.edu Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Center for Information Technology at Oberlin College invites applications for the position of Endpoint Support Specialist (Mac & Linux). This is a full-time, 12-month recurring Administrative and Professional (A&PS) staff position, reporting to the Director of IT Support. The Endpoint Support Specialist will be responsible for technical support for MacOS end-user devices and a Linux-based (Ubuntu) desktop computer lab at the College. Apple devices include laptops, desktops, and tablets. The Endpoint Support Specialist will work closely with other IT teams to ensure that end-user devices are properly maintained, configured, and secure. The ideal candidate will have experience in supporting endpoints with MacOS, Linux, and possess strong technical and customer service skills. Responsibilities Maintain and provide tier 2 technical support for all Apple devices including laptops, desktops, and tablets. Deploy new and existing Apple devices to end-users, ensuring that all are properly configured. Assist with software deployment, system updates, security patches, and OS upgrades. Responding to support tickets and requests by providing on-site or remote support. Monitor and report on endpoint performance and usage, identifying trends and areas for improvement. Collaborate with all IT teams to ensure endpoints are properly integrated with other IT systems & services. Patiently assist end-users through simple and complex issues. Assist in maintaining asset tracking and inventorying physical equipment. Provide Tier 1 support for the Linux-based computer lab environment including OS and software installation, updates, and other basic lab maintenance. Assist with Linux system administrative tasks including user access and permissions. Escalate infrastructure-related and other complex issues to system administrators. Essential Job Functions Marginal Job Functions Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, related field or equivalent work experience Minimum of 3 years of experience in IT operations while supporting many Apple devices. Strong technical skills in supporting and troubleshooting complex issues across a range of Apple devices. Strong technical knowledge of macOS, iPadOS, and native applications and features. Experience with endpoint security best practices, including encryption, antivirus and firewalls. Good understanding and technical experience with Linux-based operating systems. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and a customer service orientated approach to support. Ability to work effectively with a diverse group of stakeholders and team members. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Basic Windows technical knowledge. Desired Qualifications Industry certifications (e.g., Apple, Linux, CompTIA.) Higher Education IT experience and similar preferred. Basic familiarity automation and configuration tools such as Jamf Pro or Ansible. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17589 Compensation Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Oberlin College is committed to creating and sustaining a vibrant, welcoming community where all individuals are treated with dignity and respect, and where every member has an equal opportunity to learn, work, and contribute based on their talents, skills, and merit. We value a campus environment that draws on a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, perspectives, and ideas to enrich education, scholarship, and daily interactions. The College adheres strictly to all applicable federal and state civil rights laws, including Title VI, Title VII , Title IX, the Equal Protection Clause, and related regulations. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected characteristic in employment, admissions, or educational programs. Hiring and advancement decisions are made based on qualifications, experience, and job-related criteria. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds who share our dedication to academic excellence, free inquiry, respectful dialogue, and equal opportunity under the law to apply. The Office for Institutional Equity plays a key role in supporting a fair, compliant, and inclusive workplace and learning environment for the entire Oberlin community. Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the application on jobs.oberlin.edu Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
