    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17436": {
      "title": "Workday Technical Specialist",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Workday Technical Specialist Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Workday Technical Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Commitment to Equal Opportunity and Inclusive Excellence : Oberlin College is committed to creating and sustaining a vibrant, welcoming community where all individuals are treated with dignity and respect, and where every member has an equal opportunity to learn, work, and contribute based on their talents, skills, and merit. We value a campus environment that draws on a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, perspectives, and ideas to enrich education, scholarship, and daily interactions. The College adheres strictly to all applicable federal and state civil rights laws, including Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, the Equal Protection Clause, and related regulations. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected characteristic in employment, admissions, or educational programs. Hiring and advancement decisions are made based on qualifications, experience, and job-related criteria. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds who share our dedication to academic excellence, free inquiry, respectful dialogue, and equal opportunity under the law to apply. The Office for Institutional Equity plays a key role in supporting a fair, compliant, and inclusive workplace and learning environment for the entire Oberlin community. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary CIT invites applications for the position of Workday Technical Specialist, a key role in Oberlin’s ERP Optimization Initiative. This role is joining Oberlin at a pivotal moment, serving as the primary technical expert responsible for configuring and building the Workday platform as the College transitions from a 30-year-old Banner legacy system to a modern, cloud-based ERP that will support the institution for decades to come. Reporting to the Director of Enterprise Applications, the Workday Technical Specialist is responsible for the configuration, design, and technical build of Workday across Human Resources and Finance. This role translates business requirements into scalable, secure, and maintainable Workday configurations, ensuring alignment with institutional priorities and Workday best practices. The Workday Technical Specialist works closely with functional leads, business analysts, and integration specialists, and is expected to own the configuration integrity of the system, including business processes, security, and core platform setup. This role operates at the intersection of configuration, architecture, and integration, ensuring that Workday is built correctly from the start, with a strong technical foundation for long-term success. Responsibilities Workday Configuration & Build Ownership Design, configure, and implement Workday business processes, security models, and core system functionality. Serve as the primary owner of system configuration, ensuring consistency, quality, and alignment with Workday best practices. Establish configuration standards that support scalability, maintainability, and future enhancements. Technical Solution Design Translate functional requirements into efficient, scalable, and sustainable Workday configurations. Provide technical direction to ensure solutions are designed correctly from the outset, minimizing rework. Partner closely with Business Analysts and functional teams to ensure alignment between business needs and system capabilities. Security & Data Configuration Design and configure Workday security roles, domains, and access models. Ensure configurations align with institutional policies and data governance standards. Maintain proper structuring of sensitive HR and financial data within the system. Integration Alignment Work closely with Integration Specialists to ensure Workday configurations align with integration requirements across systems such as Banner, OnBase, CRM , and other enterprise platforms. Provide technical input into integration design to ensure compatibility with system configuration. Ensure data structures and configurations support accurate and reliable data exchange. Testing & System Validation Lead the configuration aspects of testing cycles, including unit testing, integration testing, and user acceptance testing. Ensure configurations are validated, consistent, and ready for deployment. Partner with the project team to resolve defects and ensure system quality. Configuration Quality & Continuous Improvement Continuously refine configurations to improve system performance, usability, and maintainability. Identify and correct configuration issues early to reduce downstream impact. Apply Workday best practices to ensure a clean, sustainable system design. Success Measures Success in this role will be demonstrated through: High-quality, scalable Workday configurations aligned with best practices Minimal rework due to strong upfront design and configuration discipline Well-structured security and data models supporting institutional needs Configurations that enable reliable integrations and reporting Strong contribution to testing and go-live readiness A clean, maintainable system foundation that supports long-term success Essential Job Functions Marginal Job Functions Required Qualifications Three (3) years of hands-on experience configuring Workday ( HCM & Finance) in higher education. Strong expertise in Workday business process framework and security configuration. Proven ability to translate functional requirements into technical configurations. Strong attention to detail and commitment to configuration quality. Bachelor’s degree in information technology, Business, or related field. Desired Qualifications Experience implementing Workday in a higher education or complex organizational environment. Experience working alongside integration teams in enterprise system environments. Familiarity with data governance and security frameworks. Experience supporting large-scale ERP implementations. Preferred Certifications Workday Pro HCM Certification Workday Pro Financials Certification Workday Pro Security Certification Additional certifications in Workday Integrations, Reporting, or Business Process Configuration are a plus. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17420 Compensation Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Special Instructions to Applicants Commitment to Equal Opportunity and Inclusive Excellence : Oberlin College is committed to creating and sustaining a vibrant, welcoming community where all individuals are treated with dignity and respect, and where every member has an equal opportunity to learn, work, and contribute based on their talents, skills, and merit. We value a campus environment that draws on a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, perspectives, and ideas to enrich education, scholarship, and daily interactions. The College adheres strictly to all applicable federal and state civil rights laws, including Title VI, Title VII , Title IX, the Equal Protection Clause, and related regulations. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected characteristic in employment, admissions, or educational programs. Hiring and advancement decisions are made based on qualifications, experience, and job-related criteria. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds who share our dedication to academic excellence, free inquiry, respectful dialogue, and equal opportunity under the law to apply. The Office for Institutional Equity plays a key role in supporting a fair, compliant, and inclusive workplace and learning environment for the entire Oberlin community. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17760": {
      "title": "Endpoint Support Specialist (Windows)",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Endpoint Support Specialist (Windows) Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Endpoint Support Specialist (Windows) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the application on jobs.oberlin.edu Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Center for Information Technology ( CIT ) at Oberlin College invites applications for the position of Endpoint Specialist. This is a full-time, 12-month recurring Administrative and Professional (A&PS) staff position, reporting to the Director of IT Support. The Endpoint Specialist will be responsible for managing and maintaining all Windows end-user devices at Oberlin College, including laptops, desktops, and mobile devices. The Endpoint Specialist will collaborate with other IT teams to ensure end-user devices are properly maintained, configured, and secure. The ideal candidate will have experience in managing many endpoints while possessing strong technical and customer service skills. Responsibilities Windows endpoint management including device compliance, configuration profiles, security baselines, and application packaging and deployment. Develop and implement configuration policies to ensure all end-user devices are properly configured, secured and maintained with system updates, security patches, and OS upgrades. Troubleshoot and resolve issues related to end-user devices with remote or on-site support as needed. Provide tier 3 support to technicians and the helpdesk team on complex incidents. Monitor and report on endpoint performance and usage, identifying trends and areas for improvement. Work closely with Director of IT Support to ensure that end-user devices are properly integrated with local and cloud IT systems and services. Assist with physical and virtual server-related tasks. Partner with security, networking, and helpdesk teams to standardize solutions and publish knowledge. Develop and maintain relationships with key stakeholders across CIT and the College. Essential Job Functions Marginal Job Functions Required Qualifications Associate’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, related field, or equivalent work experience. Strong technical skills in Windows endpoint management & administration including Microsoft 365 workloads. Proficient experience with management tools such as Intune, Entra ID, and 365 Admin Center. Minimum of 3 years of experience in IT operations or support and managing many endpoints. Strong understanding of endpoint security best practices, device encryption, antivirus, firewall configuration. Experience with print management systems such as Papercut. Experience in patch management and vulnerability management. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and customer service skills. Strong analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to work effectively with a diverse group of stakeholders and team members. Basic fluency with macOS support. Desired Qualifications Microsoft Certifications, CompTIA Network+, A+, Security+, PowerShell Automation, Single Sign-On solutions, Windows Server infrastructure. Higher Education IT experience and similar preferred. ITIL Foundation Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17700 Compensation Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Oberlin College is committed to creating and sustaining a vibrant, welcoming community where all individuals are treated with dignity and respect, and where every member has an equal opportunity to learn, work, and contribute based on their talents, skills, and merit. We value a campus environment that draws on a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, perspectives, and ideas to enrich education, scholarship, and daily interactions. The College adheres strictly to all applicable federal and state civil rights laws, including Title VI, Title VII , Title IX, the Equal Protection Clause, and related regulations. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected characteristic in employment, admissions, or educational programs. Hiring and advancement decisions are made based on qualifications, experience, and job-related criteria. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds who share our dedication to academic excellence, free inquiry, respectful dialogue, and equal opportunity under the law to apply. The Office for Institutional Equity plays a key role in supporting a fair, compliant, and inclusive workplace and learning environment for the entire Oberlin community. Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the application on jobs.oberlin.edu Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
