    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17658": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Photo Lab Monitor (Student Worker) Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Photo Lab Monitor (Student Worker) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Studio Art Program is seeking Photo Lab Monitors. Responsibilities Track ink inventory, assist students, maintain photo lab both digital & analogue, take inventory of photo supplies, work with the Arts Program Coordinator, Studio Media Manager to ensure lab functions properly, complete tasks from supervisor as needed Qualifications Applicant must have taken a photo class in the past. Applicant must reside in Oberlin and be currently enrolled during the semester of employment. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17657 Compensation $13.00 Special Instructions to Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously worked as a student employee in any capacity on the Oberlin College campus before? Yes No Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
