    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17304": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Living Machine Operator Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Living Machine Operator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must be an enrolled student at Oberlin College & Conservatory to qualify. A complete application will be comprised of 1) a Statement of Interest; 2) a Resume; 3) List of References Review of applications will begin on March 26th Questions about the position may be addressed to: ben.hobbs@oberlin.edu Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Environmental Studies Program will be hiring two (2) Living Machine Operators, one (1) of whom must be able to work DURING THE SUMMER OF 2026. We are seeking applicants with experience in lab sciences, demonstrated ability to work independently, and a strong work ethic. The student operators will share the responsibilities of caring for the Living Machine, as well as the building and grounds of the Adam Joseph Lewis Center ( AJLC ) and will have principal responsibilities related to: Maintaining a water quality monitoring program associated with the Living Machine and Plum Creek. Management and maintenance of the AJLC grounds and garden Responsibilities With respect to water quality monitoring, the students will help maintain the Living Machine through regularly scheduled water quality testing as well as assisting in the maintenance of the automated, real-time water quality monitoring technology for Plum Creek and effluent from the City’s Wastewater Treatment plant. A staff member or members will make bi-weekly visits to the plant to calibrate and verify the function of automated sensors that collect and display water quality data. Together with other staff, collect weekly samples from several regular sampling points along the Plum Creek and will conduct water quality analyses and assist in the development of a rating curve. Inside the Living Machine, staff collect and conduct weekly operations assessments of the health of the system, they sample water for more sophisticated testing in the lab, and they manage and maintain the vegetation in the tanks of the system. Lastly, those staff who are additionally hired to work during the summer will be responsible for garden duties, including watering, weeding, pruning, harvesting, and delivery of foodstuffs to Oberlin Community Services as well as all the responsibilities listed above. Additionally, staff will mow and edge according to a schedule, and in general aid in a continued effort to keep the AJLC looking good. Operators are also expected to participate in our Living Machine Open Hours at least three times per semester. Open Hours are held every Friday from 12:30-3:30 at the Living Machine Mini-Lab and allow interested students to drop in and ask questions or get more information about what we do. Qualifications We will be hiring two (2) operators total to start in the Spring of 2026, however one (1) new student operator must be able to continue on through the Summer of 2026. Summer work is a full 40-hour week for approximately 8 weeks. The Ideal Candidate will: • Have taken at least one laboratory science while a student at Oberlin. • Have strong interest in working as a student operator beyond the 2026-2027 academic year Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17300 Compensation New Student Operators will be paid $13.00/hr upon hiring. Special Instructions to Applicants You must be an enrolled student at Oberlin College & Conservatory to qualify. A complete application will be comprised of 1) a Statement of Interest; 2) a Resume; 3) List of References Review of applications will begin on March 26th Questions about the position may be addressed to: ben.hobbs@oberlin.edu Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Letter of Intent List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17789": {
      "title": "Office of the Dean of Students - Student Assistant",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Office of the Dean of Students - Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Office of the Dean of Students - Student Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. A complete application will be comprised of 1) a Cover Letter; 2) a Resume; 3) List of References Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The student assistant will support the daily operations in the Dean of Students Office and report to the Executive Assistant to the VP/Dean of Students and Office Manager by assisting with administrative, technological and operational tasks. This position provides an excellent opportunity to gain hands-on experience in operational processes within a higher education environment. The assistant will provide accurate and timely information by answering the office phone or greeting guests who visit the office. Additionally, this student would be expected to support the Dean of students’ office in constructing basic documents, making copies, proofreading, creating announcements, filing and scanning as directed. The ideal candidate will be reliable, detailed oriented, responsible possess strong organizational skills and the ability to work independently. Responsibilities Answer and route phone calls, greet and direct visitors Organize and maintain office records, including filing and document management. Assist office staff with events, catering, and supplies Ability to design best practice tools and templates for greater efficiency Assist with graphic design requests for high level presentation materials for organizational communication and events Office duties including stocking and inventory of supplies, sorting and distributing the mail. Conduct research and prepare materials for departmental projects and meetings. Assist with data entry and analysis. Maintain confidentiality of all student-related information. Perform other duties as assigned Qualifications Minimum Qualification: Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple tasks efficiently. Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team setting. Must be highly organized, disciplined, dependable, punctual, self-motivated, and flexible. Ability to use good judgement and to exercise discretion. Desired Qualification: Coursework or prior experience in business, accounting, or finance. Experience in an office setting or familiarity with administrative processes. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17754 Compensation $13 Special Instructions to Applicants A complete application will be comprised of 1) a Cover Letter; 2) a Resume; 3) List of References Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17505": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Wellness Ambassador Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Wellness Ambassador Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants must be certified through NASPA’s Certified Peer Educator (CPE) program before applying. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary Wellness Ambassadors serve as a resource through the Office of Health Promotion and Prevention Services and will play a crucial role in supporting fellow students by providing education, resources, and support related to mental health, wellness, and academic success. The Wellness Ambassadors will directly report to the Director of Health Promotion and Prevention Services. Responsibilities Promote mental health, substance use prevention, and holistic wellness. Collaborate with campus departments and student organizations. Represent student voices in wellness programming and outreach. Facilitate peer-led wellness workshops and events. 1:1 peer support session. Qualifications Certified through NASPA Certified Peer Educator ( CPE ) Currently enrolled and in good academic standing. Commitment to maintaining confidentiality and professionalism. Comfortable interacting with members of the college & local community across identities. Familiarity with social media Basic graphic design via Canva Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/15528 Compensation Position is for the full 26-27 academic year. Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants must be certified through NASPA’s Certified Peer Educator ( CPE ) program before applying. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17702": {
      "title": "Director of Student Engagement",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Director of Student Engagement Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Director of Student Engagement Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Director of Student Engagement is an essential member of the Division of Student Affairs at Oberlin College. This position provides leadership to the Office of Student Leadership and Involvement, while leading the overall student organization engagement strategy with an overall goal of student learning, success, and retention. The position reports directly to the Director of Student Leadership & Civic Engagement. Responsibilities The Director of Student Engagement also serves as a resource to student organizations throughout the entire life cycle of an organization, including managing the new organization chartering process, advising the “Student Finance Committee” that funds student organizations, leading Student Organization Leadership Retreats, Training Organizations and Organization Advisors, and helping with organizational leadership transitions. This position should keep track of trends of best practice in higher education, to best support our student organizations and provide high-impact engagement opportunities. Essential Job Functions Student Organizations Coordinate the student organization chartering process. Manage student organization storage, resource room, and office allocation. Serve as a resource for all student organizations. Advise the “Student Finance Committee” that allocates student organization funding. Facilitate training for the Student Organization undergraduate leadership and advisors. Organize and execute training and professional development for all student organization advisors. Maintain the virtual student organization resource guide and handbook. Assist the Student Senate and Director of Student Leadership & Civic Engagement in coordinating an annual Student Organization and Leadership Recognition and Awards event. Lead workshops, in collaboration with the Director of Student Leadership & Civic Engagement, to help navigate issues for organizations such as, but not limited to, conflict, leadership transition, and inclusive practices. Administrative Negotiate and execute event contracts on behalf of Oberlin College. Hire, train, schedule, and supervise student employees who fall under the purview of this position. Revise policies relating to the Office of Student Leadership & Involvement annually. Miscellaneous Participate in professional development organizations including, but not limited to, ACPA , NASPA , ACUI , NACA , GLCA , NODA , and COFHE . Be visible on campus to students, student organizations, and campus staff. Participate on campus committees, including for large-scale events, to help represent student organizations. Other duties as assigned. Marginal Job Functions Required Qualifications Educational Requirement: Master’s degree in Student Affairs Administration, Counseling, or other related fields. Five (5) or more years of progressive experience working in Student Affairs and, in particular, with campus programming and student organizations. Experience advising student organizations on a college campus. Prior Experience supervising both professional staff and student staff. Strong oral and written communication skills. Ability to multi-task and work on several large projects simultaneously. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and the Google Suite. Significant experience in training, team building/facilitation, co-curricular event planning, assessment, and mentoring/coaching with diverse constituencies. Experience with budget management and financial systems, including problem solving, collaboration, partnership development, and counseling/human relationships within a supervisory role. Experience with large-scale event planning. Desired Qualifications Experience advising a Student Finance Board that allocates money to campus organizations. Experience working with “Presence” Student Engagement Software Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17612 Compensation Competitive and commensurate to experience Commitment to Equal Opportunity and Inclusive Excellence : Oberlin College is committed to creating and sustaining a vibrant, welcoming community where all individuals are treated with dignity and respect, and where every member has an equal opportunity to learn, work, and contribute based on their talents, skills, and merit. We value a campus environment that draws on a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, perspectives, and ideas to enrich education, scholarship, and daily interactions. The College adheres strictly to all applicable federal and state civil rights laws, including Title VI, Title VII , Title IX, the Equal Protection Clause, and related regulations. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected characteristic in employment, admissions, or educational programs. Hiring and advancement decisions are made based on qualifications, experience, and job-related criteria. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds who share our dedication to academic excellence, free inquiry, respectful dialogue, and equal opportunity under the law to apply. The Office for Institutional Equity plays a key role in supporting a fair, compliant, and inclusive workplace and learning environment for the entire Oberlin community. Special Instructions to Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17326": {
      "title": "CHEM 102 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | CHEM 102 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry &amp; Biochemistry Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment CHEM 102 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must complete all of the “Availability” section of the application in order to be considered. Applications will be accepted until all positions are filled. Questions may be directed to Cristinel Mîinea, Laboratory Instructor and Manager, Chemistry & Biochemistry Department ( cmiinea@oberlin.edu ). Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for Teaching Assistants (TAs) for the Fall 2026 semester. There are openings for assisting CHEM 102 lab sections. Applicants must be pursuing an interest in the sciences in order to be considered (pursuing a major in chemistry or biochemistry is preferred, but not required). Chemistry & Biochemistry TAs will get the opportunity to develop their understanding of the materials at hand, gain further knowledge of topics that they previously learned, develop a professional relationship with new students, and develop their skills as educators. Responsibilities 5-8 hour/week commitment. Responsibilities include: · Prior knowledge and reasonable mastery of CHEM 102 material; · Availability to attend TA meetings taking place once weekly; · Grading laboratory assignments in a timely manner; · Assisting students in lab with relevant techniques and processes. · With the agreement of TAs and instructors, additional paid hours may be available for tutoring sessions outside of lab periods, to assist students with preparation of lab reports, other lab assignments, and review of lab-related concepts. Qualifications You must be an enrolled student at Oberlin College & Conservatory to qualify. In order to be considered, applicants must have earned a passing grade in CHEM 102 or CHEM 103. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17325 Compensation $13.00-$13.75 depending on prior TA work experience in the department. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must complete all of the “Availability” section of the application in order to be considered. Applications will be accepted until all positions are filled. Questions may be directed to Cristinel Mîinea, Laboratory Instructor and Manager, Chemistry & Biochemistry Department ( cmiinea@oberlin.edu ). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Which afternoons are you available? (M-F 1:30-4:30 pm). (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17796": {
      "title": "Research Help Desk Library Student Assistant",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Research Help Desk Library Student Assistant - Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Research Help Desk Library Student Assistant - Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Qualified applicants will be contacted to schedule an interview. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary This position is responsible for excellent customer service by providing research and library help through online chat and in person at the Research Help and Circulation desks. The job offers a great opportunity to become more familiar with the library and gain research and public service skills. Responsibilities Assist library users online and in person; answer general questions, help users locate information and conduct research Answer questions and assist library users (in-person, online, via phone), make referrals to other departments as needed, and enforce library policy Support patrons in using library equipment and applications Assist with the maintenance and activities of the Academic Commons Assist the Core Reference Team with library displays, promotion of services and collections, assessment projects, workshops, class instruction, and/or special events… Other related duties as required Qualifications Must be able to work the following shifts: Mon. 1:30-2:30pm, Wed. 2-4pm and Thurs. 7-9pm Must be enrolled at Oberlin College Public service orientation (enjoy working with people!) Basic familiarity with libraries, online library catalogues, research databases, and office equipment (photocopier, fax, scanner). Desired qualification is experience with the Oberlin College Libraries. Attention to detail and strong organizational skills Able to communicate effectively in both written and oral form Willingness to do a variety of tasks and learn a wide range of skills and processes. Clear sense of responsibility for fulfilling scheduled work assignments Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17795 Compensation Special Instructions to Applicants Qualified applicants will be contacted to schedule an interview. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What about this job interests you? (Open Ended Question) Tell us briefly about your experience using or working in libraries. (Open Ended Question) Have you worked in any Oberlin College library before?  If so, which one? (Open Ended Question) What is your expected semester and year of graduation? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17557": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Ninde Scholar Tutor Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Ninde Scholar Tutor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete this additional form https://oberlin.wufoo.com/forms/z8pdbo20idplvc/ Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Ninde College Access Program serves 7th–12th grade students in the Oberlin City School District. The program works with students who have a high financial need, and/or may be the first in their families to attend college. The role of the tutor is to provide academic support in classes that may challenge students, discuss college going and college preparation, reinforce student success, mentor students through career exploration and consistently be a presence in the scholars life. Responsibilities • Tutor 2-3 Scholars once a week (1 hour each) from September-May (Winter Term Excluded) • Proactively contact scholars in order to confirm appointments • Attend tutor meetings and trainings • Commit to tutoring for full academic year • Attend Ninde Family events as available • Serve as leader and mentor to Ninde Scholars • Gather feedback and report on success and/or areas of suggested improvement • Build strong relationships with scholars, program tutors and program facilitators • Report information (tutor log, surveys, feedback) as requested by program facilitators Qualifications • Oberlin College student • Strong writing, reading and organization skills, with an ability to follow through with commitments • Strong Math and Science background a plus • Interest in working with students in grades 7-12, from various backgrounds and ability levels • Ability to serve as a positive role model for Ninde Scholars Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/989 Compensation starting at $14 an hour with increases due to time in position and other Ninde program activities. Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete this additional form https://oberlin.wufoo.com/forms/z8pdbo20idplvc/ Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17330": {
      "title": "CHEM 211 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | CHEM 211 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry &amp; Biochemistry Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment CHEM 211 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must complete all of the “Availability” section of the application in order to be considered. Applications will be accepted until all positions are filled. Questions may be directed to Cristinel Mîinea, Chemistry & Biochemistry Laboratory Instructor and Manager (cmiinea@oberlin.edu) or Rachel Saylor, Associate Professor of Chemistry & Biochemistry (rsaylor@oberlin.edu). Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for Teaching Assistants (TAs) for the Fall 2026 semester. There are openings for assisting CHEM 211 lab sections. Applicants must be pursuing an interest in the sciences in order to be considered (pursuing a major in chemistry or biochemistry is preferred, but not required). Chemistry & Biochemistry TAs will get the opportunity to develop their understanding of the materials at hand, gain further knowledge of topics that they previously learned, develop a professional relationship with new students, and develop their skills as educators. Responsibilities 4-5 hour/week commitment. Responsibilities include: · Prior knowledge and reasonable mastery of CHEM 211 material; · Availability to attend TA meetings taking place once weekly; · Grading laboratory assignments in a timely manner; · Assisting students in lab with relevant techniques and processes. Qualifications You must be an enrolled student at Oberlin College & Conservatory to qualify. In order to be considered, applicants must have earned a minimum grade of B in CHEM 211. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17329 Compensation $13.00-$13.75 depending on prior TA work experience in the department. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must complete all of the “Availability” section of the application in order to be considered. Applications will be accepted until all positions are filled. Questions may be directed to Cristinel Mîinea, Chemistry & Biochemistry Laboratory Instructor and Manager (cmiinea@oberlin.edu) or Rachel Saylor, Associate Professor of Chemistry & Biochemistry (rsaylor@oberlin.edu). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Which afternoons are you available? (M-F 1:30-4:30 pm). (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
