    "https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17666": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Reproducible Media Print Lab Monitor Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Reproducible Media Print Lab Monitor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Qualification Applicants must have previously taken at least two Reproducible Media courses at Oberlin. Posting Details Announcement Information Job Summary The department of Studio Art is currently seeking reproducible media print lab monitors for the fall 2026 semester. Responsibilities Responsibilities Reproducible Media Print Lab Monitors are responsible for assisting students with printmaking processes, performing daily shop maintenance, and enforcing lab procedures and safety protocols. Monitors will have a set weekly schedule of 1-2 shifts that occurs outside of class time. Monitor shifts occur M-Th 7-9pm and F-Su 4-6pm. Qualifications Applicants must have previously taken at least one Reproducible Media course at Oberlin. Quick Link for Posting https://jobs.oberlin.edu/postings/17655 Compensation $13.00 Special Instructions to Applicants Qualification Applicants must have previously taken at least two Reproducible Media courses at Oberlin. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously worked as a student employee in any capacity on the Oberlin College campus before? Yes No * Have you completed at least one (1) Reproducible Media course? Please note the course, instructor, and any other Rep. Media courses you have taken if more than one. (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
